      "notifiedOn": null,
      "notes": "PNW road trip, autumn 2028. 49 nights, solo. Fly London → Seattle in, San Francisco → London home. Weekly Airbnb bases with day trips; motels on the Oregon coast nights.\n\nROUTE & DAY TRIPS\n• Seattle (25 Sep–1 Oct): car-free, light rail from the airport. Columbia Center Sky View, Pike Place + Storyville Coffee, Golden Gardens, Kerry Park, Capitol Hill, Fremont, Ballard, Discovery Park. Day trips: Poulsbo (Bremerton ferry), North Bend/Snoqualmie (Twede's, Salish Lodge), Roslyn.\n• Forks (1–8 Oct): pick up car 1 Oct, Edmonds–Kingston ferry, lunch in Port Townsend. Day trips: Lake Crescent + Mount Storm King, La Push, Hoh Rain Forest, Ruby Beach, Kalaloch, Lake Quinault, Port Angeles/Hurricane Ridge.\n• Astoria (8–15 Oct): Cannon Beach, Seaside, Cape Disappointment, Ecola, Fort Stevens.\n• Mosier / Hood River (15–22 Oct): Multnomah Falls & the Gorge, Mt Hood, Fruit Loop pumpkin patches.\n• Portland (22–25 Oct): city, Powell's, maybe a McMenamins night. Silver Falls.\n• St. Helens, base in Columbia City (25 Oct–1 Nov): Spirit of Halloweentown, festival weekend 28–29 Oct, Twilight walking tour, HALLOWEEN NIGHT Tue 31 Oct. Rideshare is scarce – plan the night home.\n• Oregon 101 (1–4 Nov): Hwy 26 to Cannon Beach, then 101 south: Manzanita, Tillamook, Three Capes, Pacific City, Lincoln City, Depoe Bay → Newport → Yachats, Cape Perpetua, Heceta Head → Florence, Hobbit Trail, Coos Bay → Bandon.\n• Trinidad (4–7 Nov): Boardman Scenic Corridor on the way in. Prairie Creek Redwoods, Fern Canyon, Ferndale, Avenue of the Giants.\n• Mendocino (7–9 Nov): 101 turns inland at Leggett – take Highway 1 down the coast.\n• San Francisco (9–13 Nov): drop the car on arrival. Golden Gate, Lands End, Alcatraz, Muir Woods, Haight & Mission.\n\nCOSTS (est. £11.3–16.9k, target ~£13.5k)\n• Accommodation £5.5–7.5k (Airbnb search, same dates 2027).\n• Car: one-way SEA → SFO, 1 Oct–9 Nov. Checked Oct 2026 for a 39-day Nov–Dec rental: RAV4 £1,117 incl. £279 one-way fee; insurance extra. Budget £1,250–1,650 with insurance + 2028 uplift. Age 25 = no young-driver fee.\n• Flights £600–1,000 · fuel £400–600 · food £1.3–2k · parks pass $250 · activities £560–910.\n\nBOOK FIRST: St. Helens-area stay as soon as autumn 2028 calendars open (~Oct–Nov 2027). Then Forks, other bases, flights ~5 months out.\n\nSAFETY: never leave anything visible in the car (SF). Never turn your back on the sea; stay off driftwood logs.",
